 {
  "title": "Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? The moderating effect of financial performance",
  "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267",
  "source": "Journal of Cleaner Production",
  "journal": "Journal of Cleaner Production",
  "journal_tier": "top",
  "date": "2019-07-01",
  "category": "literature",
  "department": "其他",
  "region": "国际",
  "quality": "C",
  "summary": "Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? The moderating effect of financial performance",
  "tags": [],
  "content_fetched": true,
  "pdf": null,
  "cid": "8e6943201ba3d660",
  "importance": 5.59,
  "added_at": "2026-10-09",
  "_ev": "ti:f1496372dad448f6",
  "quality_src": "B",
  "water_rel": 0.3,
  "kg_terms": [],
  "content_type": "研究文献",
  "kclass": "research",
  "content_class": "academic",
  "gate_status": "keep",
  "gate_reason": "学术文献（top：Journal of Cleaner Production）",
  "content": "Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? the moderating effect of financial performance\n - University of Birmingham \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Skip to main navigation \n Skip to search \n Skip to main content \n \n \n \n \n \n \n University of Birmingham Home \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Help & FAQ \n Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Search content at University of Birmingham \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Home \n \n \n \n Research output \n \n \n \n Profiles \n \n \n \n Research units \n \n \n \n Projects \n \n \n \n Activities \n \n \n \n Datasets \n \n \n \n Equipment \n \n \n \n Prizes \n \n \n \n Press/Media \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? the moderating effect of financial performance \n Tiansen Liu , Yufeng Zhang , Dapeng Liang \n Management \n \n Research output : Contribution to journal › Article › peer-review \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 14 \n \n Citations\n(Scopus) \n \n \n \n \n 660 \n Downloads\n(Pure) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Overview \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Fingerprint \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Abstract \n There is a growing debate on how should Chinese manufacturing firms improve their environmental performance (EP). In this paper, we analyze the impact of ownership structure (OS, including ownership property, SOP; ownership concentration, H5; shareholding ratio of the largest and second shareholders, FS; total proportion of stated-owned shares owned by top 10 shareholders, TOP10; proportion of independent directors accounting for all board members, ID) on EP with the consideration of the moderating effect of financial performance measured by net profit rate (NPR) through surveying 1605 firm-year observations. The findings present that the overall EP of Chinese manufacturing firms is relatively low (The average level is only 25.94% of the ideal maximum). Both SOP and H5 significantly improve EP (marginal effects within 8.20%~8.76% and 4.37%~4.44%, respectively), while the impacts of FS and TOP10 are both not significantly positive. Additionally, H5 significantly improves EP (8.90%~9.08%) when TOP10 is higher, and SOP significantly improves EP (10.01%~10.86%) when TOP10 is lower. Further, NPR negatively moderates the impact of FS on EP for the full sample and only positively moderates the impact of higher TOP10 on EP. However, the weak moderating effect of NPR also releases a positive signal fhat the level of EP is not dominated by financial performance. Accordingly, corporate EP may keep rising based on its prior trend instead of a major volatility in the coming period. \n Original language English Pages (from-to) 58-71 Journal Journal of Cleaner Production Volume 225 Early online date 29 Mar 2019 DOIs https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267 Publication status Published - 10 Jul 2019 \n \n \n \n \n UN SDGs \n This output contributes to the following UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n SDG 12 \n Responsible Consumption and Production \n \n \n \n \n \n Keywords Ownership structure—OS Environmental performance—EP Financial performance—FP Net profit rate—NPR Corporate social responsibility—CSR Environmental management capability—EMC \n \n \n \n Access to Document \n 10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267 Licence: None: All rights reserved Tiansen_Liu_et_al_Can_ownership_structure_affect_environmental_performance_Journal_of_Cleaner_Production_2019 Checked for eligibility: 29/03/2019 Accepted author manuscript, 700 KB Licence: Creative Commons: Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivs (CC BY-NC-ND) https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0959652619309771 Licence: None: All rights reserved \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Fingerprint \n \n \n Dive into the research topics of 'Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? the moderating effect of financial performance'. Together they form a unique fingerprint.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Moderating Effect \n Keyphrases \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Environmental Performance \n Keyphrases \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Ownership Structure \n Keyphrases \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Financial Performance \n Keyphrases \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Chinese Manufacturing Firms \n Keyphrases \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Chinese \n Social Sciences \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Profit Rate \n Social Sciences \n 100% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Volatility \n Social Sciences \n 33% \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n View full fingerprint\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Cite this \n \n \n \n APA\n \n \n \n Author\n \n \n \n BIBTEX\n \n \n \n Harvard\n \n \n \n Standard\n \n \n \n RIS\n \n \n \n Vancouver\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Liu, T. , Zhang, Y. , & Liang, D. (2019). Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? the moderating effect of financial performance . Journal of Cleaner Production , 225 , 58-71. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267 \n \n \n \n Liu, Tiansen ; Zhang, Yufeng ; Liang, Dapeng. / Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? the moderating effect of financial performance . In: Journal of Cleaner Production . 2019 ; Vol. 225. pp. 58-71. \n \n \n \n @article{4fef82508d1a4658b12e091394b8cac6, title = \"Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms?: the moderating effect of financial performance\", abstract = \"There is a growing debate on how should Chinese manufacturing firms improve their environmental performance (EP). In this paper, we analyze the impact of ownership structure (OS, including ownership property, SOP; ownership concentration, H5; shareholding ratio of the largest and second shareholders, FS; total proportion of stated-owned shares owned by top 10 shareholders, TOP10; proportion of independent directors accounting for all board members, ID) on EP with the consideration of the moderating effect of financial performance measured by net profit rate (NPR) through surveying 1605 firm-year observations. The findings present that the overall EP of Chinese manufacturing firms is relatively low (The average level is only 25.94\\% of the ideal maximum). Both SOP and H5 significantly improve EP (marginal effects within 8.20\\%\\textasciitilde{}8.76\\% and 4.37\\%\\textasciitilde{}4.44\\%, respectively), while the impacts of FS and TOP10 are both not significantly positive. Additionally, H5 significantly improves EP (8.90\\%\\textasciitilde{}9.08\\%) when TOP10 is higher, and SOP significantly improves EP (10.01\\%\\textasciitilde{}10.86\\%) when TOP10 is lower. Further, NPR negatively moderates the impact of FS on EP for the full sample and only positively moderates the impact of higher TOP10 on EP. However, the weak moderating effect of NPR also releases a positive signal fhat the level of EP is not dominated by financial performance. Accordingly, corporate EP may keep rising based on its prior trend instead of a major volatility in the coming period. \", keywords = \"Ownership structure—OS, Environmental performance—EP, Financial performance—FP, Net profit rate—NPR, Corporate social responsibility—CSR, Environmental management capability—EMC\", author = \"Tiansen Liu and Yufeng Zhang and Dapeng Liang\", year = \"2019\", month = jul, day = \"10\", doi = \"10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267\", language = \"English\", volume = \"225\", pages = \"58--71\", journal = \"Journal of Cleaner Production\", issn = \"0959-6526\", publisher = \"Elsevier Korea\", } \n \n \n \n Liu, T , Zhang, Y & Liang, D 2019, ' Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? the moderating effect of financial performance ', Journal of Cleaner Production , vol. 225, pp. 58-71. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267 \n \n \n \n Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? the moderating effect of financial performance. / Liu, Tiansen ; Zhang, Yufeng ; Liang, Dapeng. In: Journal of Cleaner Production , Vol. 225, 10.07.2019, p. 58-71. Research output : Contribution to journal › Article › peer-review \n \n \n \n TY - JOUR T1 - Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? T2 - the moderating effect of financial performance AU - Liu, Tiansen AU - Zhang, Yufeng AU - Liang, Dapeng PY - 2019/7/10 Y1 - 2019/7/10 N2 - There is a growing debate on how should Chinese manufacturing firms improve their environmental performance (EP). In this paper, we analyze the impact of ownership structure (OS, including ownership property, SOP; ownership concentration, H5; shareholding ratio of the largest and second shareholders, FS; total proportion of stated-owned shares owned by top 10 shareholders, TOP10; proportion of independent directors accounting for all board members, ID) on EP with the consideration of the moderating effect of financial performance measured by net profit rate (NPR) through surveying 1605 firm-year observations. The findings present that the overall EP of Chinese manufacturing firms is relatively low (The average level is only 25.94% of the ideal maximum). Both SOP and H5 significantly improve EP (marginal effects within 8.20%~8.76% and 4.37%~4.44%, respectively), while the impacts of FS and TOP10 are both not significantly positive. Additionally, H5 significantly improves EP (8.90%~9.08%) when TOP10 is higher, and SOP significantly improves EP (10.01%~10.86%) when TOP10 is lower. Further, NPR negatively moderates the impact of FS on EP for the full sample and only positively moderates the impact of higher TOP10 on EP. However, the weak moderating effect of NPR also releases a positive signal fhat the level of EP is not dominated by financial performance. Accordingly, corporate EP may keep rising based on its prior trend instead of a major volatility in the coming period. AB - There is a growing debate on how should Chinese manufacturing firms improve their environmental performance (EP). In this paper, we analyze the impact of ownership structure (OS, including ownership property, SOP; ownership concentration, H5; shareholding ratio of the largest and second shareholders, FS; total proportion of stated-owned shares owned by top 10 shareholders, TOP10; proportion of independent directors accounting for all board members, ID) on EP with the consideration of the moderating effect of financial performance measured by net profit rate (NPR) through surveying 1605 firm-year observations. The findings present that the overall EP of Chinese manufacturing firms is relatively low (The average level is only 25.94% of the ideal maximum). Both SOP and H5 significantly improve EP (marginal effects within 8.20%~8.76% and 4.37%~4.44%, respectively), while the impacts of FS and TOP10 are both not significantly positive. Additionally, H5 significantly improves EP (8.90%~9.08%) when TOP10 is higher, and SOP significantly improves EP (10.01%~10.86%) when TOP10 is lower. Further, NPR negatively moderates the impact of FS on EP for the full sample and only positively moderates the impact of higher TOP10 on EP. However, the weak moderating effect of NPR also releases a positive signal fhat the level of EP is not dominated by financial performance. Accordingly, corporate EP may keep rising based on its prior trend instead of a major volatility in the coming period. KW - Ownership structure—OS KW - Environmental performance—EP KW - Financial performance—FP KW - Net profit rate—NPR KW - Corporate social responsibility—CSR KW - Environmental management capability—EMC U2 - 10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267 DO - 10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267 M3 - Article SN - 0959-6526 VL - 225 SP - 58 EP - 71 JO - Journal of Cleaner Production JF - Journal of Cleaner Production ER - \n \n \n \n Liu T , Zhang Y , Liang D. Can ownership structure improve environmental performance in Chinese manufacturing firms? the moderating effect of financial performance . Journal of Cleaner Production . 2019 Jul 10;225:58-71. Epub 2019 Mar 29. doi: 10.1016/j.jclepro.2019.03.267 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Powered by Pure Link opens in a new tab , Scopus Link opens in a new tab & Elsevier Fingerprint Engine&trade; Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n All content on this site: Copyright &copy; 2026 University of Birmingham, its licensors, and contributors. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies. For all open access content, the relevant licensing terms apply\n \n We use cookies to help provide and enhance our service and tailor content. By continuing you agree to the use of cookies \n \n \n Log in to Pure Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n \n \n University of Birmingham data protection policy Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n About web accessibility Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Report vulnerability Link opens in a new tab \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Contact us",
