ution of Organic Compounds in 732 \nAqueous Aerosols Collected from Above Sewage Aeration Tanks. Aerosol Science and Technology 733 \n2000; 32: 404-420. 734 \nLepri L, Desideri P, Del Bubba M . Analysis of organic pollutants in a wastewater treatment plant. Ann. 735 \nChim. 1997; 87: 317-335. 736 \nLiu Z, Li Q, Wu Q, Kuo DTF, Chen S, Hu X, et al. Removal Efficiency and Risk Assessment of Polycyclic 737 \nAromatic Hydrocarbons in a Typical Municipal Wastewater Tr eatment Facility in Guangzhou, 738 \nChina. International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health 2017; 14: 861. 739 \n28 \n \nLoyo-Rosales JE, Rice CP, Torrents A. Fate of Octyl- and Nonylphenol Ethoxylates and Some Carboxylated 740 \nDerivatives in Three American Wastewater Treatment Plants. Environmental Science & Technology 741 \n2007; 41: 6815-6821. 742 \nManoli E, Samara C. Occurrence and Mass Balance of Polycyclic Aromatic Hydrocarbons in the 743 \nThessaloniki Sewage Treatment Plant. Journal of Environmental Quality 1999; 28: 176-187. 744 \nManoli E, Samara C. The removal of Polycyclic Aromatic Hydrocarbons in the wastewater treatment 745 \nprocess: Experimental calculations and model predictions. Environmental Pollution 2008; 151: 477 -746 \n485. 747 \nMartínez-Alcalá I, Guillén -Navarro JM, Fernández -López C. Pharmaceutical biological degradation, 748 \nsorption and mass balance determination in a conventional activated -sludge wastewater treatment 749 \nplant from Murcia, Spain. Chemical Engineering Journal 2017; 316: 332-340. 750 \nMasi F, Lepri L, Del Bubba M, Sacco C, Lo Nostro A, Comodo N. Organic chemicals and microbial facies 751 \nof liquid aerosols from a wastewater treatment plant. Annali di chimica 1999; 89: 231-248. 752 \nMcAdam EJ, Bagnall JP, Soares A, Koh YK, Chiu TY, Scrimshaw MD, et al. Fate of alkylphenolic 753 \ncompounds du ring activated sludge treatment: impact of loading and organic composition. 754 \nEnvironmental science & technology 2010; 45: 248-254. 755 \nMe