  "title": "Monitoring irrigation water use over paddock scales using climate data and landsat observations",
  "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.agwat.2019.05.002",
  "source": "Agricultural Water Management",
  "journal": "Agricultural Water Management",
  "journal_tier": "top",
  "date": "2019-07-01",
  "category": "tech",
  "department": "其他",
  "region": "国际",
  "quality": "C",
  "summary": "Monitoring irrigation water use over paddock scales using climate data and landsat observations",
  "tags": [],
  "content_fetched": true,
  "pdf": null,
  "cid": "a22b4a7b0b3f6501",
  "importance": 5.59,
  "added_at": "2026-10-09",
  "_ev": "ti:599df7262e9789b7",
  "quality_src": "B",
  "water_rel": 0.3,
  "kg_terms": [],
  "content_type": "研究文献",
  "kclass": "research",
  "content_class": "academic",
  "gate_status": "keep",
  "gate_reason": "学术文献（top：Agricultural Water Management）",
  "content": "Item - Monitoring irrigation water use over paddock scales using climate data and landsat observations - Open Research Newcastle - Figshare Skip to main content Browse Browse and Search Search Monitoring&#32;irrigation&#32;water&#32;use&#32;over&#32;paddock&#32;scales&#32;using&#32;climate&#32;data&#32;and&#32;landsat&#32;observations https://hdl.handle.net/1959.13/1402197 Open external identifier URL Copy identifier URL to clipboard Identifier Info Cite Download ( 4.63 MB ) Share Embed journal&#32;contribution posted on 2025-05-10, 15:23 authored by David&#32;Bretreger , In-Young&#32;Yeo In-Young Yeo , Juan&#32;Quijano , John&#32;Awad , Gregory&#32;Hancock Gregory Hancock , Gary&#32;Willgoose Irrigated&#32;agriculture&#32;has&#32;been&#32;identified&#32;as&#32;using&#32;approximately&#32;72&#37;&#32;of&#32;water&#32;globally.&#32;Many&#32;regions&#32;of&#32;the&#32;world&#32;are&#32;subject&#32;to&#32;water&#32;sharing&#32;plans&#32;that&#32;cross&#32;government&#32;boarders&#32;which&#32;contain&#32;a&#32;mixture&#32;of&#32;management&#32;policies,&#32;leading&#32;to&#32;the&#32;requirement&#32;to&#32;monitor&#32;irrigation&#32;water&#32;use.&#32;The&#32;study&#32;reported&#32;here&#32;aims&#32;to&#32;develop&#32;and&#32;test&#32;an&#32;approach&#32;using&#32;Landsat&#32;observations&#32;to&#32;monitor&#32;irrigation&#32;water&#32;use&#32;over&#32;paddock&#32;scales&#32;without&#32;the&#32;need&#32;for&#32;in-situ&#32;observations,&#32;ground&#32;data&#32;or&#32;knowledge&#32;of&#32;planting&#32;dates.&#32;Using&#32;conservative&#32;assumptions&#32;about&#32;agricultural&#32;land&#32;management&#32;practice&#32;&#40;i.e.&#32;negligible&#32;runoff,&#32;drainage&#32;and&#32;soil&#32;moisture&#32;change&#41;,&#32;the&#32;irrigation&#32;is&#32;calculated&#32;over&#32;25&#8201;m&#8201;x&#8201;25&#8201;m&#32;Landsat&#32;images.&#32;The&#32;approach&#32;uses&#32;a&#32;combination&#32;of&#32;three&#32;vegetation&#32;indices&#32;derived&#32;from&#32;Landsat&#32;images&#32;to&#32;calculate&#32;crop&#32;coefficients&#32;&#40;K&#60;sub&#62;c&#60;&#47;sub&#62;&#41;&#32;based&#32;on&#32;multiple&#32;published&#32;relationships.&#32;These&#32;are&#32;combined&#32;through&#32;the&#32;FAO56&#32;methodology&#32;using&#32;gridded&#32;rainfall&#32;and&#32;two&#32;gridded&#32;reference&#32;evapotranspiration&#32;&#40;ET&#60;sub&#62;o&#60;&#47;sub&#62;&#41;&#32;products&#32;to&#32;estimate&#32;actual&#32;evapotranspiration,&#32;providing&#32;six&#32;K&#60;sub&#62;c&#60;&#47;sub&#62;&#32;-&#32;ET&#60;sub&#62;o&#60;&#47;sub&#62;&#32;combinations&#32;which&#32;are&#32;then&#32;compared&#32;to&#32;actual&#47;recorded&#32;irrigation&#32;volumes&#32;from&#32;test&#32;sites.&#32;The&#32;method&#32;was&#32;tested&#32;over&#32;an&#32;almond&#32;farm,&#32;two&#32;vineyards&#32;and&#32;a&#32;cotton&#32;field&#59;&#32;in&#32;addition&#32;to&#32;Goulburn-Murray&#32;Water&#8217;s&#32;&#40;GMW&#41;&#32;individual&#32;farm&#32;scale&#32;sites&#32;with&#32;unknown&#32;crops,&#32;all&#32;located&#32;within&#32;Australia.&#32;The&#32;developed&#32;approach&#32;provided&#32;estimated&#32;irrigation&#32;volumes&#32;that&#32;closely&#32;matched&#32;measured&#32;data&#32;for&#32;almond&#32;and&#32;cotton&#32;farms,&#32;while&#32;vineyards&#32;returned&#32;less&#32;accurate&#32;results&#32;due&#32;to&#32;localised&#32;management&#32;techniques&#32;that&#32;do&#32;not&#32;agree&#32;with&#32;land&#32;management&#32;assumptions&#32;made.&#32;The&#32;results&#32;from&#32;GMW&#32;showed&#32;some&#32;indication&#32;of&#32;the&#32;irrigation&#32;water&#32;use,&#32;although&#32;more&#32;details&#32;of&#32;the&#32;site&#32;being&#32;assessed&#32;needs&#32;to&#32;be&#32;available&#32;&#40;i.e.&#32;crop&#32;type&#32;and&#32;extent&#41;.&#32;This&#32;study&#32;demonstrates&#32;the&#32;ability&#32;of&#32;certain&#32;remote&#32;sensing&#32;K&#60;sub&#62;c&#60;&#47;sub&#62;&#32;relationships&#32;for&#32;sensing&#32;irrigation&#32;water&#32;use&#32;and&#32;shows&#32;the&#32;potential&#32;applications&#32;of&#32;the&#32;developed&#32;approach&#32;in&#32;monitoring&#32;irrigation&#32;over&#32;paddock&#32;scale&#32;environments. History Related Materials 1. DOI - Is published in https&#58;&#47;&#47;doi.org&#47;10.1016&#47;j.agwat.2019.05.002 2. ISSN - Is version of https&#58;&#47;&#47;portal.issn.org&#47;resource&#47;ISSN&#47;0378-3774 Language en,&#32;English College/Research Centre Faculty&#32;of&#32;Engineering&#32;and&#32;Built&#32;Environment School School&#32;of&#32;Engineering Rights statement &#169;&#32;2019.&#32;This&#32;manuscript&#32;version&#32;is&#32;made&#32;available&#32;under&#32;the&#32;CC-BY-NC-ND&#32;4.0&#32;license&#32;http&#58;&#47;&#47;creativecommons.org&#47;licenses&#47;by-nc-nd&#47;4.0&#47;. Journal title Agricultural&#32;Water&#32;Management Volume 221 Issue 20&#32;July&#32;2019 Pagination 175-191 Publisher Elsevier Usage metrics views downloads citations Learn more about usage metrics Publications Categories Physical&#32;geography&#32;and&#32;environmental&#32;geoscience Keywords irrigation compliance Murray-Darling&#32;basin water&#32;resource&#32;management remote&#32;sensing SDG&#32;6 Sustainable&#32;Development&#32;Goals Licence CC&#32;BY-NC-ND&#32;4.0 Export Metadata Download Contact About Manage research outputs Library research support Copyright Privacy Acknowledgement Cookie Settings Disclaimer Sitemap fig share . credit for all your research.",
