 {
  "title": "RETRACTED ARTICLE: Triangular nexus between foreign direct investment, international tourism, and energy consumption in the Chinese economy: accounting for environmental quality",
  "url": "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11356-019-05542-y",
  "source": "Environmental Science and Pollution Research",
  "journal": "Environmental Science and Pollution Research",
  "journal_tier": "top",
  "date": "2019-06-25",
  "category": "intl_region",
  "department": "其他",
  "region": "国际",
  "quality": "C",
  "summary": "RETRACTED ARTICLE: Triangular nexus between foreign direct investment, international tourism, and energy consumption in the Chinese economy: accounting for environmental quality",
  "tags": [],
  "content_fetched": true,
  "pdf": "kb/pdf/14babf14d4405e1c.pdf",
  "cid": "14babf14d4405e1c",
  "importance": 5.59,
  "added_at": "2026-10-09",
  "_ev": "ti:192624c29ad69a6b",
  "quality_src": "B",
  "water_rel": 0.3,
  "kg_terms": [],
  "content_type": "研究文献",
  "kclass": "research",
  "content_class": "academic",
  "gate_status": "keep",
  "gate_reason": "学术文献（top：Environmental Science and Pollution Research）",
  "content": "Triangular nexus between foreign direct investment, international tourism, and energy consumption in the Chinese economy: accounting for environmental quality \n \n \n \n \n Skip to main content\n Communities & Collections All of DSpace Statistics Search Tools Request/Question English Türkçe Log In Log in New user? Click here to register. Have you forgotten your password? Home 00 Research Outputs | WoS | Scopus | TR-Dizin | PubMed WoS Indexed Publications Collection Triangular nexus between foreign direct investment, international tourism, and energy consumption in the Chinese economy: accounting for environmental quality Triangular nexus between foreign direct investment, international tourism, and energy consumption in the Chinese economy: accounting for environmental quality Loading... Date 2019 Authors Udemba, Edmund Ntom Journal Title Journal ISSN Volume Title Publisher Springer Heidelberg Access Rights info:eu-repo/semantics/closedAccess Abstract Recently, China is named among the most carbon dioxide (CO2)-emitting countries in the world after the United State of America (USA). A major part of Chinese carbon dioxide emissions is as a result of offshore industrial activities which come into the economy as foreign direct investment (FDI). Following this, the present study seeks to investigate the nexus between CO2 emissions, FDI, energy use, and tourism arrivals, and possibly to advise on who will bear the responsibility of offshore CO2 emissions. Utilizing ARDL-bound testing and Granger causality approaches for both short- and long-run effects the author found that economic growth (GDP) has a positive relationship with both tourism arrivals, energy use, FDI, and CO2.This contributes to heavy CO2 emissions which the author classified as the outsourced/offshore CO(2)emissions in China's FDI. Tourism arrivals have a bi-directional (feedback) causal relationship with energy use and a uni-directional causal relationship with CO2(transmitting from tourism to CO2). Both FDI and energy use have a bi-directional (feedback) causal relationship; CO2, energy use, and tourism arrivals have a unidirectional relationship with GDP which established the triangular nexus causality among the variables and the impact on GDP. Hence, the policy implication should be geared towards implementing the policies and regulations that will checkmate and reduce the excesses of foreign firms to the environment quality of China and promote environmentally friendly economic activities. Description Keywords CO2 emissions , Energy use , FDI , Tourism arrivals , Offshore activities , Economic growth , China Journal or Series Environmental Science and Pollution Research WoS Q Value N/A Scopus Q Value Q1 Volume 26 Issue 24 Citation URI https://doi.org/10.1007/s11356-019-05542-y https://hdl.handle.net/11129/11932 Collections WoS Indexed Publications Collection PubMed Indexed Publications Collection Scopus İndeksli Yayınlar Koleksiyonu Endorsement Review Supplemented By Referenced By Full item page | Eastern Mediterranean University | Library | Guide | OAI-PMH | Jisc |\n This site is protected by Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivs 4.0 Unported License .\n Eastern Mediterranean University, Özay Oral Library, Famagusta, North Cyprus via Mersin 10, TÜRKİYE If you find any errors in content please report us DSpace 9.2 Powered by İdeal DSpace DSpace software copyright © 2002-2026 LYRASIS Cookie settings Accessibility settings Privacy policy End User Agreement Send Feedback COAR Notify",
  "content_kind": "fulltext",
  "fulltext_status": "已获取全文",
  "fulltext_source": "Unpaywall(HTML)",
  "fulltext_chars": 3517,
  "fulltext_tried_at": "2026-10-12"
 },
