 {
  "title": "MFC-based biosensor for domestic wastewater COD assessment in constructed wetlands",
  "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2018.12.347",
  "source": "Science of The Total Environment",
  "journal": "Science of The Total Environment",
  "journal_tier": "top",
  "date": "2019-04-01",
  "category": "tech",
  "department": "其他",
  "region": "国际",
  "quality": "C",
  "summary": "MFC-based biosensor for domestic wastewater COD assessment in constructed wetlands",
  "tags": [],
  "content_fetched": true,
  "pdf": null,
  "cid": "29cd8bc5c001d697",
  "importance": 5.59,
  "added_at": "2026-10-10",
  "_ev": "ti:4e88b1393a4565ae",
  "quality_src": "B",
  "water_rel": 0.3,
  "kg_terms": [],
  "content_type": "研究文献",
  "kclass": "research",
  "content_class": "academic",
  "gate_status": "keep",
  "gate_reason": "学术文献（top：Science of the Total Environment）",
  "content": "[2003.14078] MFC-based biosensor for domestic wastewater COD assessment in constructed wetlands \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Skip to main content \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Search\n \n Submit \n Donate \n \n Log in \n \n \n \n \n \n Search arXiv \n \n \n \n \n \n Press Enter to search &middot; Advanced search \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n--> \n \n \n Quantitative Biology > Quantitative Methods \n \n \n arXiv:2003.14078 (q-bio)\n \n \n \n \n \n [Submitted on 31 Mar 2020] \n Title: MFC-based biosensor for domestic wastewater COD assessment in constructed wetlands \n Authors: C. Corbella , M. Hartl , M. Fernandez-gatell , J. Puigagut (Group of environmental engineering and microbiology (GEMMA), Universitat Politecnica de Catalunya - BarcelonaTech) View a PDF of the paper titled MFC-based biosensor for domestic wastewater COD assessment in constructed wetlands, by C. Corbella and 4 other authors \n View PDF \n \n Abstract: In the context of natural-based wastewater treatment technologies (such as constructed wetlands - CW) the use of a low-cost, continuous-like biosensor tool for the assessment of operational conditions is of key importance for plant management optimization. The objective of the present study was to assess the potential use of constructed wetland microbial fuel cells (CW-MFC) as a domestic wastewater COD assessment tool. For the purpose of this work four lab-scale CW-MFCs were set up and fed with pre-settled domestic wastewater at different COD concentrations. Under laboratory conditions two different anodic materials were tested (graphite rods and gravel). Furthermore, a pilot-plant based experiment was also conducted to confirm the findings previously recorded for lab-scale experiments. Results showed that in spite of the low coulombic efficiencies recorded, either gravel or graphite-based anodes were suitable for the purposes of domestic wastewater COD assessment. Significant linear relationships could be established between inlet COD concentrations and CW-MFC Ecell whenever contact time was above 10 hours. Results also showed that the accuracy of the CW-MFC was greatly compromised after several weeks of operation. Pilot experiments showed that CW-MFC presents a good bio-indication response between week 3 and 7 of operation (equivalent to an accumulated organic loading between 100 and 200 g COD/m2, respectively). Main conclusion of this work is that of CW-MFC could be used as an &#34;alarm-tool&#34; for qualitative continuous influent water quality assessment rather than a precise COD assessment tool due to a loss of precision after several weeks of operation.\n \n \n \n \n Comments: \n 46 pages, 14 Figures \n \n \n Subjects: \n \n Quantitative Methods (q-bio.QM) \n \n Cite as: \n arXiv:2003.14078 [q-bio.QM] \n \n \n \n (or \n arXiv:2003.14078v1 [q-bio.QM] for this version)\n \n \n \n \n https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2003.14078 \n \n \n Focus to learn more \n \n \n \n arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite \n \n \n \n Journal reference: \n 660, 2019, 218-226 \n \n \n \n Related DOI :\n \n https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2018.12.347 \n \n \n \n \n Focus to learn more \n \n \n \n \n DOI(s) linking to related resources\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Submission history From: Marco Hartl [ view email ] [v1] \n Tue, 31 Mar 2020 10:30:42 UTC (808 KB) \n \n \n \n \n \n Full-text links: \n Access Paper: \n \n \nView a PDF of the paper titled MFC-based biosensor for domestic wastewater COD assessment in constructed wetlands, by C. Corbella and 4 other authors View PDF \n \n \n view license \n \n \n \n Current browse context: \n q-bio.QM \n \n \n < prev \n \n | \n next > \n \n \n new \n | \n recent \n | 2020-03 \n \n Change to browse by:\n \n q-bio \n \n \n \n \n References & Citations \n \n NASA ADS Google Scholar \n Semantic Scholar \n \n \n \n \n export BibTeX citation \n Loading... \n \n 