mental variable. Scientific reports, 7(1), p.12777. 432 \nFaraway, J.J., 2016. Extending the linear model with R: generalized linear, mixed effects and nonparametric 433 \nregression models (Vol. 124). CRC press. 434 \nFolmer O., M. Black, W. Hoeh, R. Lutz, and R. Vrijenhoek. 1994. DNA primers for amplification of mitochondrial 435 \ncytochrome c oxidase subunit I from diverse metazoan invertebrates. Molecular Marine Biology and 436 \nBiotechnology. 3:294-297. 437 \nGibson, J.F., Shokralla, S., Curry, C., Baird, D.J., Monk, W.A., King, I. and Hajibabaei, M., 2015. Large-scale 438 \nbiomonitoring of remote and threatened ecosystems via high -throughput sequencing. PloS one, 10(10 ), 439 \np.e0138432. 440 \nGonzález-Tortuero E., J. Rusek, A. Petrusek, S. Gießler, D. Lyras, S. Grath, F. Castro -Monzón, and J. 441 \nWolinska. 2015. The quantification of representative sequences pipeline for amplicon sequencing: case 442 \nstudy on within-population its1 sequence variation in a microparasite infecting daphnia. Molecular Ecology 443 \nResources. 15:1385-1395. 444 \nGotelli, N.J. and Chao, A., 2013. Measuring and estimating species richnes s, species diversity, and biotic 445 \nsimilarity from sampling data. 446 \nHajibabaei M., S. Shokralla, X. Zhou, G. A. C. Singer, and DJ Baird. 2011. Environmental barcoding: A next-447 \ngeneration sequencing approach for biomonitoring applications using river benthos. PLoS ONE. 6:e17497. 448 \nHajibabaei M., J. L. Spall, S. Shokralla, and S. van Konynenburg. 2012. Assessing biodiversity of a freshwater 449 \nbenthic macroinvertebrate community through non -destructive environmental barcoding of DNA from 450 \npreservative ethanol. BMC Ecology. 12:28. 451 \n.CC-BY-NC-ND 4.0 International licenseavailable under a \nnot certified by peer review) is the author/funder, who has granted bioRxiv a license to display the preprint in perpetuity. It is made \nThe copyright holder for this preprint (which wasthis version posted October 5, 2018. ;