  "content": "Item - Overlap in fish assemblages observed using pelagic and benthic baited remote underwater video stations - figshare - Figshare Research that keeps its context. Writing, analysis, code, and AI in one research workspace. Start for free Skip to main content Browse Browse and Search Search Overlap&#32;in&#32;fish&#32;assemblages&#32;observed&#32;using&#32;pelagic&#32;and&#32;benthic&#32;baited&#32;remote&#32;underwater&#32;video&#32;stations https://hdl.handle.net/10536/DRO/DU:30154812 Open external identifier URL Copy identifier URL to clipboard Identifier Info Cite Share Version 2 Version 2 2024-06-05, 04:57 Version 2 2024-06-05, 04:57 Version 1 2019-01-01, 00:00 Version 1 2019-01-01, 00:00 journal&#32;contribution posted on 2024-06-05, 04:57 authored by TM&#32;Clarke , Sasha&#32;Whitmarsh Sasha Whitmarsh , PG&#32;Fairweather , C&#32;Huveneers Baited&#32;remote&#32;underwater&#32;video&#32;stations&#32;&#40;BRUVS&#41;&#32;are&#32;increasing&#32;in&#32;popularity&#32;as&#32;non-invasive&#32;and&#32;fishery-independent&#32;tools&#32;for&#32;assessing&#32;fish&#32;assemblages.&#32;Although&#32;most&#32;BRUVS&#32;studies&#32;have&#32;focused&#32;on&#32;benthic&#32;fish&#32;communities,&#32;recent&#32;studies&#32;also&#32;use&#32;BRUVS&#32;to&#32;examine&#32;the&#32;comparatively&#32;undersampled&#32;pelagic&#32;communities.&#32;However,&#32;the&#32;propensities&#32;of&#32;benthic&#32;BRUVS&#32;to&#32;detect&#32;pelagic&#32;fishes&#32;and,&#32;likewise,&#32;pelagic&#32;BRUVS&#32;to&#32;detect&#32;demersal&#32;fishes&#32;are&#32;unknown.&#32;This&#32;study&#32;simultaneously&#32;used&#32;benthic&#32;and&#32;pelagic&#32;BRUVS&#32;deployed&#32;either&#32;separately&#32;&#40;single&#41;&#32;or&#32;in&#32;combination&#32;to&#32;determine&#32;assemblages&#32;of&#32;demersal&#32;and&#32;pelagic&#32;species&#32;at&#32;three&#32;contrasting&#32;sites&#32;within&#32;temperate&#32;South&#32;Australia.&#32;Assemblages&#32;observed&#32;by&#32;benthic&#32;v.&#32;pelagic&#32;BRUVS&#32;differed&#32;significantly&#32;at&#32;all&#32;sites,&#32;including&#32;one&#32;as&#32;shallow&#32;as&#32;7m&#32;deep,&#32;but&#32;there&#32;were&#32;no&#32;significant&#32;differences&#32;in&#32;assemblages&#32;observed&#32;between&#32;BRUVS&#32;of&#32;the&#32;same&#32;position&#32;&#40;i.e.&#32;pelagic&#32;or&#32;benthic&#41;&#32;when&#32;BRUVS&#32;were&#32;deployed&#32;as&#32;single&#32;units&#32;or&#32;in&#32;combination.&#32;This&#32;study&#32;reveals&#32;the&#32;limitations&#32;of&#32;using&#32;only&#32;benthic&#32;or&#32;pelagic&#32;BRUVS,&#32;and&#32;highlights&#32;the&#32;necessity&#32;for&#32;both&#32;BRUVS&#32;positions&#32;to&#32;be&#32;used&#32;together&#32;to&#32;ensure&#32;that&#32;a&#32;comprehensive&#32;representation&#32;of&#32;entire&#32;fish&#32;assemblages&#32;throughout&#32;the&#32;water&#32;column&#32;can&#32;be&#32;obtained. History Related Materials 1. DOI - Is version of https&#58;&#47;&#47;doi.org&#47;10.1071&#47;MF18224 Location Clayton,&#32;Vic. Language English Publication classification C1.1&#32;Refereed&#32;article&#32;in&#32;a&#32;scholarly&#32;journal Journal Marine&#32;and&#32;Freshwater&#32;Research Volume 70 Pagination 870-880 ISSN 1323-1650 eISSN 1448-6059 Issue 6 Publisher CSIRO&#32;PUBLISHING Usage metrics views downloads citations Learn more about usage metrics Research Publications Categories No categories selected Keywords Science&#32;&#38;&#32;Technology Life&#32;Sciences&#32;&#38;&#32;Biomedicine Physical&#32;Sciences Fisheries Limnology Marine&#32;&#38;&#32;Freshwater&#32;Biology Oceanography communities demersal MaxN monitoring&#32;methods multivariate&#32;analysis water&#32;column REEF&#32;FISH HABITAT&#32;ASSOCIATIONS NEW-ZEALAND ABUNDANCE ECOLOGY COUNTS BRUVS Licence All&#32;Rights&#32;Reserved Export Metadata Download About Solutions Tools Blog Contact Help Privacy Policy Terms Cookie Settings Sitemap facebook page X page vimeo page fig share . credit for all your research.",
