n Guiñez M, Valdéz J, Sifeddine A, 2010. \nVariabilidad espacial y temporal de la materia orgánica sedimentaria, asociada a la Zona de Mínimo Oxígeno (ZMO), en un ambiente costero del norte de la corriente de Humboldt, bahía de Mejillones, Chile. Lat. Am. J. Aquat. Res\n38(2), 242–253. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ibarra-García EC, Ortiz M, Ríos-Jara E, Cupul-Magaña AL, Hernández-Flores Á, Rodríguez-Zaragoza F, 2016. \nThe functional trophic role of whale shark ( Rhincodon typus ) in the northern Mexican Caribbean: network analysis and ecosystem development. Hydrobiologia. 792 (1), 121–135. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Jørgensen SE, 1992. \nIntegration of Ecosystem Theories: A Pattern. Kluwer Academic Publishers, the\nNetherlands. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Jørgensen SE, Patten BC, Straskraba M, 2000. \nEcosystems emerging: 4. growth. Ecol. Modell\n126, 249–284. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Jørgensen SE, Xu F, Marques J, Salas F, 2005. \nApplication of indicators for the assessment of ecosystem health Pages 6–65 in Jørgensen S, editor. Handbook of ecological indicators for assessment of ecosystem health. CRC Press, Boca Raton, Florida, USA: Jørgensen, S.E., Nielsen, S.N., 2014. Use of eco-exergy in ecological network. Ecol. Modell. 293, 202–209. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Kaufman A, Borrett S, 2010. \nEcosystem network analysis indicators are generally robust to parameter uncertainty in a phosphorus model of Lake Sidney Lanier, USA. Ecol. Modell\n221, 1230–1238. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Levins R, 1966. \nThe strategy of model building in population biology. Am. Sci\n54 (4), 421–431. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Li L, Lu H, Campbell DE, Ren H, 2010. \nEmergy algebra: Improving matrix methods for calculating transformities. Ecol. Modell\n221, 411–422. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Li L, Lu H, Tilley D, Ren H, Shen W, 2013. \nThe maximum empower principle: An invisible hand controlling the self-organizing development of forest plantations in south China. Ecol. Indic\n29, 278–292. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Linderman RL, 1942. \nThe Trophic-Dynamic Aspect of Ecology. Ecology. 23 (4), 399–417. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Liu G, Chang Z, Chen B, Ulgiati S, 2011. \nMonitoring trends of urban development and environmental impact of Beijing, 1999–2006. Sci. Total. Environ\n409 (18), 3295–3308. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Lu Y, Wang R, Zhang Y, Su H, Wang P, Jenkins A, Ferrier RC, Bailey M, Squire G, 2015. \nEcosystem health towards sustainability. Ecosystem Health and Sustainability. 1 (1), 1–15. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Lotka AJ, 1922a. \nContribution to the Energetics of Evolution. Proceeding of the National Academy of Sciences of the United Stated of America. 8, 147–151. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Lotka AJ, 1922b. \nNatural selection as a physical principle. Proceeding of the National Academy of Sciences of the United Stated of America. 8, 151–155. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Lotka AJ, 1925. \nElements of Physical Biology. Williams & Wilking, Baltimore, USA. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Marín V, Rodriguez L, Vallejo L, Fuenteseca J, Oyarce E, 1993. \nEfectos de la surgencia costera sobre la productividad primaria primaveral de Bahía Mejillones del Sur (Antofagasta, Chile). Rev. Chil. Hist. Nat\n66, 479–491. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Marín V, Olivares G, 1999. \nEstacionalidad de la productividad primaria en Bahía Mejillones del Sur (Chile): una aproximación proceso - funcional. Rev. Chil. Hist. Nat\n72, 629–641. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Marín A, Escribano R, Delgado LE, Olivares G, Hidalgo P, 2001. \nNearshore circulation in a coastal upwelling site off the Northern Humboldt current system. Cont. Shelf. Res\n21, 1317–1329. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Marín A, Delgado LE, Escribano R, 2003. \nUpwelling shadows at Mejillones Bay (northern Chilean coast): a remote sensing in situ analysis. Invest. Mar. Valparaíso\n31 (2), 47–55. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Moraga-Opazo J, Valle-Levinson A, Ramos M, Pizarro-Koch M, 2011. \nUpwellingtriggered near-geostrophic recirculation in an equatorward facing embayment. Cont. Shelf. Res\n31, 1991–1999. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Moreno RA, Sepúlveda RD, Badano EI, Thatje S, Rozbacylo N, Carrasco FD, 2008. \nSubtidal macrozoobenthos communities from northern Chile during and post El Niño 1997 – 1998. Helgoland Mar. Res\n62 (Supplement 1), 45–55. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Odum EP, 1969. \nThe strategy of ecosystem development. Science\n164, 262–270. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Odum HT, 1988. \nSelf-Organization, transformity, and information. Science. 242, 1132–1139. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Odum HT, 1994. \nEcological and general system: An introduction to systems ecology. Revised edition, University press Colorado. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Odum HT, 1996. \nEnvironmental accounting: Emergy and decision making. John Wiley and Sons, New York. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Odum HT, 2000. \nEmergy evaluation of salmon pen culture\nPresented at International Institute of Fisheries Economics and Trade. Microbehavior, Macroresults, and Externalities: Conceptual Issues 10–15. Oregon State University, Corvallis, OR. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Odum HT, Copeland BJ, MacMahan EA, 1974. \nCoastal Ecological Systems of the United States. Conservation Foundation; \nWashington, DC. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ortiz M, Wolff M, 2002. \nTrophic models of four benthic communities in Tongoy Bay (Chile): comparative analysis and preliminary assessment of management strategies. J. Exp. Mar. Biol. Ecol\n268, 205–235. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ortiz M, 2008. \nMass balanced and dynamic simulations of trophic models of kelp ecosystems near the Mejillones Peninsula of northern Chile (SE Pacific): comparative network structure and assessment of harvest strategies. Ecol. Modell\n216, 31–46. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ortiz M, Berrios F, Campos L, Uribe R, Ramírez A, Hermosillo-Núñez B, González J, Rodríguez-Zaragoza F, 2015. \nMass balanced trophic models and shortterm dynamical simulations for benthic ecological systems of Mejillones and Antofagasta bays (SE Pacific): Comparative network structure and assessment of human impacts. Ecol. Modell\n309, 153–162. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ortiz M, Berrios F, González J, Rodríguez-Zaragoza F, Gómez I, 2016. \nMacroscopic network properties and short-term dynamic simulations in coastal ecological systems at Fildes Bay (King George Island, Antarctica). Ecol. Complexity\n28, 145–157. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Oviatt C, Smith L, McManus MC, Hyde K\n2015. \nDecadal patterns of westerly winds, temperatures, ocean gyre circulations and fish abundance: A review. Climate\n3, 855–857. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Patten BC, 1995. \nNetwork integration of ecological extremal principles: exergy, emergy, power, ascendency, and indirect effects. Ecol. Modell\n79(1), 75–84. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Patricio J, Ulanowicz R, Pardal MA, Marquez JC, 2006, Ascendency as ecological indicator for environmental quality assessment at the ecosystem level: a case study. Hidrobiologia. 555, 19–30. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Rutland J, Montecino V, 2002. \nMultiscale upwelling forcing cycles and biological response off north-central Chile. Rev. Chil. Hist. Nat\n75, 217–231. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Su MR, Yang ZF, Chen B, 2010. \nRelative urban ecosystem health assessment: a method integrating comprehensive evaluation and detailed analysis. EcoHealth. 7(4), 459–472. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Strubs PT, Mesias J, Montecino V, Rutland J, 1998. \nCoastal ocean circulation off western South America. In: Robinson A, Brink K (Eds.), The Sea II. John Wiley and Sons, New York. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Tarazona J, Arntz W, Canahuire E, 1996. \nmpact of two ‘ l iño’ events of different intensity on the hypoxic soft bottom macrobenthos off central Peruvian coast. Mar. Ecol\n17, 425–446. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Taylor H, Wolff M, Mendo J, Yamashiro C, 2008. \nChanges in trophic flow structure of Independence Bay (Peru) over an ENSO cycle. Prog. Oceanogr\n79,336–351. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ulanowicz R, 1986. \nGrowth and Development Ecosystems Phenomenology. Springer; –Verlag, New York. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ulanowicz R, 1997. \nEcology, the Ascendent Perspective\nComplexity in Ecological System Series, Columbia University Press, New York. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ulanowicz R, Abarca-Arenas L, 1997. \nAn informational synthesis of ecosystem structure and function. Ecol. Modell\n95, 1–10. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Ulgiati S, Brown MT, 2002. \nQuantifying the environmental support for dilution and abatement of process emissions: The case of electricity production. J. Clean. Prod\n10, 335–348. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Valdés J, Román D, Rivera L, Morales T, Cortés P, 2011. \nMetal contents in coastal waters of San Jorge Bay, Antofagasta, northern Chile: a base line for establishing seawater quality guidelines. Environ. Monit. Assess\n183, 231–242. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Valdés J, Guiñez M, Castillo A, Vega S, 2014. \nCu, Pb and Zn content in sediments and benthic organisms from (northern Chile): accumulation and biotransference in subtidal coastal systems. Cienc. Mar\n40 (1), 45–58. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Valle-Levinson A, Moraga J, Olivares J, Blanco JL, 2000. \nTidal and residual circulation in a semi-arid bay: Coquimbo Bay, Chile. Cont. Shelf. Res\n20(15), 2009–2028. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Vargas C, Narváez D, Piñones A, Venegas R, Navarrete S, 2004. \nInternal tidal bore warm fronts and settlement of invertebrates in central Chile. Estuar. Coast. Shelf. S\n61, 603–612. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Vasallo P, Fabiano M, Vezzulli L, Sandulli R, Marques JC, Jorgensen SE, 2006. \nAssessing the health of coastal marine ecosystems: A holistic approach base on sediment micro and meio-benthic measures. Ecol. Indic\n6(3), 525–542. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Vassallo P, Paoli Ch., Fabiano M, 2009. \nEmergy required for the complete treatment of municipal wastewater. Ecol. Eng\n35, 687–694. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n Zarbá L, Brown MT, 2015. \nCycling emergy: computing emergy in trophic networks. Ecol. Modell\n315, 37–4. [ Google Scholar ] \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ACTIONS \n \n \n \n \n \n View on publisher site \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n PDF (1.0 MB) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Cite \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Collections \n \n \n \n \n \n Permalink \n \n \n \n \n PERMALINK \n \n \n \n \n Copy \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n RESOURCES \n \n \n \n \n Similar articles\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Cited by other articles\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Links to NCBI Databases\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Cite \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Copy \n \n \n \n \n \n Download .nbib \n .nbib \n \n \n \n \n \n Format: \n \n \n \n AMA\n \n \n \n APA\n \n \n \n MLA\n \n \n \n NLM\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Add to Collections \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Create a new collection \n \n \n \n Add to an existing collection \n \n \n \n \n \n Name your collection\n * \n \n \n \n \n \n Choose a collection\n \n \n \n \n Unable to load your collection due to an error \n Please try again \n \n \n \n \n \n Add\n \n \n Cancel\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Follow NCBI\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n NCBI on X (formerly known as Twitter) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n NCBI on Facebook \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n NCBI on LinkedIn \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n NCBI on GitHub \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n NCBI RSS feed \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Connect with NLM\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n NLM on X (formerly known as Twitter) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n NLM on Facebook \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n NLM on YouTube \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n National Library of Medicine\n 8600 Rockville Pike Bethesda, MD 20894 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Web Policies\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n FOIA\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n HHS Vulnera