 {
  "title": "Sediment connectivity linked to vegetation using UAVs: High-resolution imagery for ecosystem management",
  "url": "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scitotenv.2019.03.399",
  "source": "Science of The Total Environment",
  "journal": "Science of The Total Environment",
  "journal_tier": "top",
  "date": "2019-06-01",
  "category": "management",
  "department": "其他",
  "region": "国际",
  "quality": "C",
  "summary": "Sediment connectivity linked to vegetation using UAVs: High-resolution imagery for ecosystem management",
  "tags": [],
  "content_fetched": true,
  "pdf": null,
  "cid": "16db3e162890d5a8",
  "importance": 5.59,
  "added_at": "2026-10-10",
  "_ev": "ti:d365af21f37ab5ed",
  "quality_src": "B",
  "water_rel": 0.3,
  "kg_terms": [],
  "content_type": "研究文献",
  "kclass": "research",
  "content_class": "academic",
  "gate_status": "keep",
  "gate_reason": "学术文献（top：Science of the Total Environment）",
  "content": "Item - Sediment connectivity linked to vegetation using UAVs: High-resolution imagery for ecosystem management - figshare - Figshare Research that keeps its context. Writing, analysis, code, and AI in one research workspace. Start for free Skip to main content Browse Browse and Search Search Sediment&#32;connectivity&#32;linked&#32;to&#32;vegetation&#32;using&#32;UAVs&#58;&#32;High-resolution&#32;imagery&#32;for&#32;ecosystem&#32;management https://hdl.handle.net/102.100.100/517666 Copy identifier URL to clipboard Identifier Info Cite Share journal&#32;contribution posted on 2023-05-24, 04:14 authored by Estrany,&#32;J , Ruiz,&#32;M , Calsamiglia,&#32;A , Marc&#32;Carriqui&#32;Alcover , Garcia-Comendador,&#32;J , Nadal,&#32;M , Fortesa,&#32;J , Lopez-Tarazon,&#32;JA , Medrano,&#32;H , Gago,&#32;J In&#32;this&#32;study,&#32;a&#32;low-cost&#32;unmanned&#32;aerial&#32;vehicle&#32;was&#32;used&#32;to&#32;obtain&#32;multi-spectral&#32;high-resolution&#32;imagery&#32;&#40;1.4&#32;cm&#32;px&#60;sup&#62;-1&#60;&#47;sup&#62;&#41;&#32;from&#32;2&#32;microcatchments&#32;&#40;3.3&#32;ha&#41;&#32;with&#32;burned&#32;Mediterranean&#32;shrubland&#32;and&#32;pine&#32;forests.&#32;This&#32;imagery&#32;was&#32;used&#32;to&#32;calculate&#32;the&#32;blue&#32;normalized&#32;differential&#32;vegetation&#32;index&#32;and&#32;to&#32;generate&#32;digital&#32;elevation&#32;models&#32;for&#32;estimating&#32;the&#32;sediment&#32;connectivity&#32;index.&#32;Both&#32;indices&#32;enabled&#32;an&#32;integrated&#32;approach&#32;for&#32;deciphering&#32;how&#32;hydrological&#32;and&#32;sediment&#32;connectivity&#32;interact&#32;with&#32;vegetation&#32;as&#32;well&#32;as&#32;soil&#32;conservation&#32;structures.&#32;The&#32;application&#32;of&#32;spatial&#32;analysis&#32;improves&#32;our&#32;understanding&#32;of&#32;the&#32;feedback&#32;between&#32;biological&#32;and&#32;geomorphological&#32;processes.&#32;Local&#32;spatial&#32;data&#32;analysis&#32;established&#32;a&#32;significant&#32;link&#32;between&#32;local&#32;geomorphological&#32;and&#32;biological&#32;factors,&#32;enabling&#32;a&#32;precise&#32;identification&#32;of&#32;homogeneous&#32;areas&#32;at&#32;micro-catchment&#32;scale&#32;and&#32;the&#32;minimal&#32;size&#32;of&#32;vegetation&#32;units&#32;reacting&#32;to&#32;geomorphology&#32;as&#32;natural&#32;groups&#32;at&#32;plot-scale&#32;where&#32;management&#32;strategies&#32;and&#32;efforts&#32;should&#32;be&#32;applied.&#32;Establishing&#32;this&#32;local&#32;relationship&#32;between&#32;sediment&#32;connectivity&#32;and&#32;vegetation&#32;patterns&#32;through&#32;new&#32;and&#32;interdisciplinary&#32;methodologies&#32;represents&#32;a&#32;new&#32;strategy&#32;for&#32;the&#32;assessment&#32;of&#32;ecosystem&#32;dynamics&#32;and&#32;management. History Related Materials 1. DOI - Is supplement to Sediment&#32;connectivity&#32;linked&#32;to&#32;vegetation&#32;using&#32;UAVs&#58;&#32;High-resolution&#32;imagery&#32;for&#32;ecosystem&#32;management Publication title Science&#32;of&#32;the&#32;Total&#32;Environment Volume 671 Pagination 1192-1205 ISSN 0048-9697 Department/School School&#32;of&#32;Natural&#32;Sciences Publisher Elsevier&#32;Science&#32;Bv Place of publication Po&#32;Box&#32;211,&#32;Amsterdam,&#32;Netherlands,&#32;1000&#32;Ae Rights statement Copyright&#32;2019&#32;Elsevier&#32;B.V. Socio-economic Objectives Assessment&#32;and&#32;management&#32;of&#32;freshwater&#32;ecosystems&#59;&#32;Expanding&#32;knowledge&#32;in&#32;the&#32;biological&#32;sciences&#59;&#32;Expanding&#32;knowledge&#32;in&#32;the&#32;earth&#32;sciences Repository Status Restricted Usage metrics views downloads citations Learn more about usage metrics University Of Tasmania Categories Plant&#32;physiology Surface&#32;water&#32;hydrology Environmental&#32;management Environmental&#32;management Keywords ecogeomorphology Mediterranean&#32;shrubland burned&#32;areas UAVs BNDVI sediment&#32;connectivity Licence In&#32;Copyright Export Metadata Download About Solutions Tools Blog Contact Help Privacy Policy Terms Cookie Settings Sitemap facebook page X page vimeo page fig share . credit for all your research.",
  "content_kind": "fulltext",
  "fulltext_status": "已获取全文",
  "fulltext_source": "Unpaywall(HTML)",
